  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/assets/c66cdc8bbddfb00ce69f843b1ce1d12116b2dd82312a34abafa0fb13907110cf.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of $\\mathbb{R}^3?$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I  represents a plane that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is a subspace of  $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\n\n- Diagram II  represents a line that passes through the origin. Therefore, it is also a subspace of  $\\mathbb{R}^3.$\n\n- Diagram III does not represent a subspace. The origin ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14045249/assets/a80f685053d7ac3f868728be13b5651c15bfb6c8f8f4394df75256b750a67485.png)  clearly lies outside the subset.\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"",
